A card database other processes read while one serves it (Commander Duels v0.9.10, game isolation).
Every format.

Reason: since v0.9.10 each game runs in a Java process of its own (docs/engine/isolation.md). The
engine's front process opens the cards database first; XMage opens it with AUTO_SERVER, so every game
process started after it reads the cards through it on loopback and holds no copy of its own. But
opening the repositories writes: CardRepository and ExpansionRepository each check the database's
version and build (inserting a row when it is not there) and create their table if it does not
exist. A game process starting while another reads (a deck being imported, a card created by name)
took the schema's lock, and the other's query failed ("can't find any cards") or waited. A process
started with -Dxmage.cardsDatabase.shared=true takes the database as the front process opened it:
no checks, no table created, nothing written. The front process itself, and every engine that is not
isolated, opens it as before.

Remove when: XMage opens its repositories without writing, or the engine stops sharing one database
between processes.

